}
```

In this example, the lambda function `square` is defined to square a number. The `std::transform` function is then used to apply this lambda to each element in the `numbers` vector, storing the results in the `results` vector. This approach allows you to run the same code (squaring a number) inline on multiple named variables (the elements of the `numbers` vector).

